	'ppl_h1' => 'Henrik Lund, Master Mason',
	'ppl_p1' => 'Master mason Henrik Lund spent three years on scaffolding inside Warehouse No. 7 between 2016 and 2019. When the exterior walls required stabilization, Henrik insisted on repairing the brick bays individually rather than applying modern facings. He methodically sourced matching historic bricks from a collapsed loading shed nearby on Pier 7, examining each piece by hand. His masonry crew repointed thousands of joints using traditional lime mortar mixed to match the original 1924 formula. Henrik’s meticulous craft preserved the rough, patinated texture of the façade, ensuring that the warehouse retains its historic maritime dignity for generations to come.',
	'ppl_h2' => 'Mirela Costa, Head Concierge',
	'ppl_p2' => 'Head concierge Mirela Costa is the person who greets guests at Door 7 as evening settles over the water. Arriving at Soko Hotel, visitors are met by Mirela sliding open the heavy steel-framed entrance onto the quiet reception hall. Having lived by Vessa Harbour for decades, she guides arrivals to the best morning walks along the quayside, coordinates ferry crossings, and ensures every stay begins with unhurried calm. Mirela believes hospitality lies in small, thoughtful gestures—remembering a guest’s preference for tea, preparing extra wool blankets before cold harbour winds rise, or quietly orienting travellers to the rhythm of the port.',
	'ppl_h3' => 'Pavel Novak, Night Porter',
