	'res_title' => 'Reserve',
	'res_intro' => 'Reservations at Soko Hotel are handled directly by our front desk team without third-party booking engines. We hold requested rooms personally to ensure every stay is tailored with care.',
	'res_form_h' => 'Write to reserve',
	'res_form_lede' => 'Tell us your arrival date, number of nights, guests and room type. We reply within one working day.',
	'res_k1' => 'Holding Period and Cancellation Policy',
	'res_v1' => 'We do not use automated booking widgets or third-party reservation networks. When you inquire about dates, our staff temporarily reserves your room for 48 hours, giving you ample time to coordinate travel arrangements before confirming. Once a reservation is confirmed, our cancellation policy allows full refunds up to seven days prior to your scheduled arrival date. Cancellations made within seven days of check-in, or no-shows, will incur a charge equivalent to the first night of the stay. For modifications, please contact our reservations desk directly by telephone or email.',
	'res_k2' => 'Inquiry Details and Contact Direct',
	'res_v2' => 'To assist us in preparing your reservation, please include your preferred arrival date, number of nights, total guests, and desired room type—whether Harbour Room, Quay Double, Loft Suite, or Crane Suite. If you have dietary preferences for breakfast at the Canteen or require late check-out until 15:00, mentioning this in your initial message allows us to accommodate your needs immediately. Our reservations line is open daily from 09:00 to 19:00 at +00 20 555 0147, and all written correspondence should be directed to stay@sokohotel.example.',
	'con_kicker' => 'Reception 24 hours',
	'con_title' => 'Contact',
	'con_intro' => 'Whether you have questions regarding an upcoming stay, require harbour directions, or wish to arrange a private event, our team at Warehouse No. 7 is here to assist.',
	'con_form_h' => 'Write to the reception',
	'con_form_lede' => 'Questions about a stay, harbour directions or a private event: we reply to every message within one working day.',
	'con_k1' => 'Telephone',
	'con_v1' => '+00 20 555 0147, reservations daily 09:00–19:00',
	'con_k2' => 'Email',
	'con_v2' => 'stay@sokohotel.example',
	'con_k3' => 'Address',
	'con_v3' => 'Pier 7, Kessel Quay 14, Vessa Harbour',
	'con_k4' => 'Reception',
	'con_v4' => 'Open 24 hours a day',
	'con_h1' => 'Front Desk and Direct Channels',
	'con_p1' => 'The reception desk at Soko Hotel is staffed 24 hours a day to welcome arriving guests and handle immediate inquiries. For general questions, room reservations, or travel advice, you may reach our staff by telephone at +00 20 555 0147. The dedicated reservations phone line operates daily between 09:00 and 19:00. Alternatively, email us anytime at stay@sokohotel.example. We make it a rule to review incoming messages continuously and reply to every written inquiry within one working day, providing thoughtful and comprehensive guidance for your visit.',
	'con_h2' => 'Press, Architecture, and Private Events',
	'con_p2' => 'Inquiries regarding architectural photography, editorial coverage, or private gatherings in the Canteen should be addressed directly to our management team. General manager Tomas Adeyemi oversees event arrangements, while founder Ines Varga handles architectural documentation and design press queries. Due to the quiet nature of Warehouse No. 7 and the comfort of our overnight residents, we host a strictly limited number of small cultural gatherings, book launches, and dinners each season. Please send your event proposal and timing requirements to stay@sokohotel.example with the subject line clearly marked for management review.',
	'con_h3' => 'Finding Door 7 on Kessel Quay',
	'con_p3' => 'Soko Hotel is located at Pier 7, Kessel Quay 14, Vessa Harbour. When arriving on the quay by foot, tram, or water ferry, look for the tall arched brick bays of Warehouse No. 7 facing the dockside. The entrance is marked as Door 7, situated at the ground floor waterline. The entrance features blackened-steel frames and our discreet bay stamp. Should you require immediate assistance locating the building or finding parking upon arrival, call our front desk directly at +00 20 555 0147, and a concierge will gladly guide you to the door.',
	'nws_kicker' => 'Four times a year',
	'nws_title' => 'Newsletter',
	'nws_intro' => 'A letter from the quay, four times a year. We share quiet reflections on harbour life, seasonal menus from the Canteen, and notes on ongoing restoration work at Warehouse No. 7.',
	'nws_form_h' => 'A letter from the quay',
	'nws_get_h' => 'What you receive',
	'nws_k1' => 'From the Canteen',
	'nws_v1' => 'Seasonal notes, new dishes and the producers who supply them, introduced by Noor Haddad.',
	'nws_k2' => 'From the building',
	'nws_v2' => 'Stories of the brick, the crane beam and the repairs that never quite end, by Ines Varga and Henrik Lund.',
	'nws_k3' => 'From the harbour',
	'nws_v3' => 'Tides, shipping and quiet events along Kessel Quay, as Pavel Novak sees them from the night desk.',
	'nws_a_h' => 'Our Approach to Correspondence',
	'nws_a_p' => 'We hold a deep respect for quiet communication, in our hotel and in your digital mailbox. Soko Hotel does not send marketing promotions, seasonal flash discounts, or automated sales sequences. When you subscribe, you receive exactly four issues a year, written directly by our staff members in the same reflective tone as our daily life on Pier 7. We hope each letter serves as a calm pause in your day, bringing the steady atmosphere of the harbour and the honest warmth of our warehouse to your desk, wherever you may be.',
	'nws_p_h' => 'Privacy and Subscription Terms',
	'nws_p_p' => 'Your email address is stored securely and used exclusively for transmitting the quarterly Soko Hotel newsletter. We never sell, share, or disclose your contact details to third parties, external marketing agencies, or commercial tracking services. Submitting the subscription form opens your email application with a pre-formatted subscription request to stay@sokohotel.example. Every quarterly message contains a clear, one-click unsubscribe mechanism, allowing you to withdraw your subscription at any time without friction. For any questions regarding your personal information, our front office is always available to assist.',
	'hsn_kicker' => 'Quiet hours 22:00–07:00',
	'hsn_title' => 'House Notes',
	'hsn_intro' => 'To preserve the quiet, contemplative atmosphere of Warehouse No. 7, we ask all guests to observe a few essential house guidelines during their stay on Kessel Quay.',
	'hsn_k1' => 'Are children welcome at Soko Hotel?',
	'hsn_v1' => 'Children of all ages are warmly welcomed at Soko Hotel. Because Warehouse No. 7 is an authentic 1924 industrial conversion featuring open mezzanine stairs and hard surfaces, we ask parents to supervise young children thoughtfully. Loft Suites and Crane Suites offer ample room for families, and baby cots or extra beds can be arranged in advance upon request. Our Harbour Rooms and Quay Doubles are designed specifically for one or two adult occupants and cannot accommodate extra rollaway beds. Please notify our reservations desk when booking so we can prepare your family\'s room comfortably.',
	'hsn_k2' => 'Are pets permitted to stay in the hotel?',
	'hsn_v2' => 'Pets and animals are not permitted inside Soko Hotel or the Canteen dining room. While we appreciate animal companionship, this policy protects the historic oiled timber floors, wool blankets, and restored brick surfaces of Warehouse No. 7, as well as the comfort of guests with severe allergies. Certified assistance animals accompanying guests with disabilities are permitted in full accordance with applicable regulations. If you are travelling with a certified service animal, kindly inform our reservations team at stay@sokohotel.example prior to arrival so we can allocate a suitable room on an accessible floor.',
	'hsn_k3' => 'Is Warehouse No. 7 accessible for all guests?',
	'hsn_v3' => 'The ground floor of Warehouse No. 7—including Door 7, the reception hall, and the Canteen—is fully step-free and accessible from Kessel Quay. An elevator provides level access to guest rooms located on the first, second, and third floors, including all eighteen Harbour Rooms, eight Quay Doubles, and four Loft Suites. Please note that the two top-floor Crane Suites are located beneath the roof framing and require navigating an interior flight of stairs; consequently, they are not wheelchair accessible. Accessible bathrooms feature roll-in showers with grab rails and level thresholds throughout the designated rooms.',
	'hsn_k4' => 'What are the hotel quiet hours?',
	'hsn_v4' => 'Quiet hours are observed throughout Soko Hotel each evening between 22:00 and 07:00. Given the open spatial qualities and brick construction of Warehouse No. 7, sound carries easily along the corridors and high ceilings. We kindly ask guests to speak softly in common hallways, keep room audio devices at low volumes, and close steel doors gently during these nocturnal hours. Our night porter Pavel Novak is on duty throughout the night to assist with quiet arrivals and ensure all residents enjoy undisturbed rest beside the water of Vessa Harbour.',
	'journal_intro' => 'The Soko Hotel journal records stories of craft, architecture, and daily life along Kessel Quay. It gathers archival notes and personal reflections from the team that restored and runs Warehouse No. 7.',
	// END inner
);
